    "comment": "MngB is an \u03b1-mannosidase that appears to be responsible for the conversion of 2-O-(6-phospho-\u03b1-mannosyl)-D-glycerate (MG-P) to mannose-6-phosphate and glycerate in the 2-O-\u03b1-mannosyl-D-glycerate degradation pathway [Sampaio04].  The enzyme has not yet been purified and assayed in vitro. \n\nExpression of mngAB is repressed by MngR and induced when cells are grown in 2-O-\u03b1-mannosyl-D-glycerate (MG).  mngB mutants are unable to grow in medium containing high levels of MG (without secondary mutations in mngA), likely due to the toxicity of accumulating MG-P within the cells [Sampaio04].\n\nMngB: \"mannosylglycerate catabolism B\" [Sampaio04]"
  },
